<div class="g-prose"><p>Easing is <code>ease-standard</code>, <code>{{ t.transitionTimingFunction.standard }}</code>, and the default for every transition.</p></div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="distance-scaled">Distance-scaled</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>Two scripts time their own motion. <code>expandable.js</code> gives a full expansion the whole <code>--expand-base</code> duration and a partial reversal a share of it, so stopping half-way does not take as long as the full move. <code>cite_cta.js</code> holds a touch press for <code>--cta-span</code> so a quick tap is still seen. Both are covered by <code>tools/motion.test.cjs</code> in the app.</p></div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="reduced-motion">Reduced motion</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The feature styles imported by <code>styles.css</code> include reduced-motion rules; <code>adaptive-overrides.css</code> keeps the shared <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> override late in the cascade. Reader passage scrolling uses <code>scrollBehavior()</code> in <code>composables/highlight.js</code>, so they jump instead of gliding:</p></div>
{{ code("code-scroll", "assets/js/alpine/composables/highlight.js", "function scrollBehavior() {
  return window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'instant' : 'smooth';
}

target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: scrollBehavior(), block: 'start' });") }}
{{ note("Nothing essential appears only during an animation: a toast's text is in a live region, and a flashed passage stays highlighted long enough to find without the flash.") }}
